# GameUIEditer

Figma-like game UI editor for art teams. Output is a structured document JSON (Figma-file equivalent) for AI / PixiJS / React consumers.

## Stack (locked)

- Monorepo: `apps/editor`, `packages/atlas`, `packages/document`
- React 19 + Vite + TypeScript + Tailwind 4
- **PixiJS v8** for canvas (matches AI Studio game runtime)
- React for chrome only (panels, toolbar, dialogs)
- Zustand for editor UI state; Document is source of truth
- Local-first (localStorage / file export); cloud share later

## Architecture

- `packages/document`: node tree, schema, commands, undo/redo, serialize
- `packages/atlas`: sprite pack/trim/nine-slice/import-export (from Sprite sheet packer)
- `apps/editor`: UI shell + Pixi scene sync
- Mutations go through **Commands** only (never mutate document ad-hoc in components)
- Export contract: `GET`-style document JSON + atlas assets (Figma REST API analog)

## Design canvas

- Default design size: **1280×720**
- Presets: landscape 1280×720, portrait 720×1280
- Adaptive aspect **16:9 → 21:9** (portrait: height adaptive up to **720×1560**)
- Nine-slice sprites must render via Pixi nine-slice (or equivalent)

## Rules

- Keep modules decoupled; no God stores that mix atlas + canvas + network
- No hardcoded user-facing Chinese/English strings without a key map when i18n lands; P0 may use Chinese labels
- Do not rewrite `Sprite sheet packer/` in place — evolve `packages/atlas`
- Prefer production-ready code; no TODO placeholders in shipped paths
